DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/materia-roundtable-discussion
 -on-the-microphysics-of-power-beyond-the-human\n\nOn our yearly theme: Mic
 ropower and the Non-human: Micropower\, or the microphysics of power\, is 
 a category established by Foucault early on in his thinking\, before his t
 urn towards biopolitics. In Discipline and Punish (1975)\, Foucault posits
  that the microphysics of power’s “field of validity is situated in a 
 sense between [state apparatuses] and the bodies themselves with their mat
 eriality and their forces.” (26).If\, on the one hand\, we understand bo
 dies in an expanded sense\, without privileging the human \,and\, on the o
 ther\, we probe in de facto contemporary state apparatuses from the bottom
  up(algorithmic governance\, corporate takeover of attention span\, etc.)\
 , we find multiple opportunities to intervene. We would like to rekindle t
 he spirit of the original formulation\, revise Foucault\, and set him into
  conversation with different archives\, in keeping with the group’s orie
 ntation\, Latin Americanist and otherwise. \n\nStay tuned for our exciting
  announcement of speakers!
END:VEVENT
